hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15670","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have praised my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, with praises and eulogies, and you. He said: Bring what you praised your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, with. He said: So I began reciting to him, and a dark man came and sought permission. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be silent, be silent. He said: So he spoke a while then left. He said: So I began reciting to him. He said: Then he came and sought permission. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be silent, be silent. So he did that two or three times. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who is this for whom you silenced me. He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. This is a man who does not love falsehood."
"15671","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not recite to you praises I praised my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, with. He said: Indeed your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, loves praise."
"15672","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin and al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a prisoner, and he said: O Allah, I repent to You and do not repent to Muhammad. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He knew the right to its people."
"15673","Yunus narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a detachment on the day of Hunayn, and they fought the polytheists, and killing led them to offspring. When they came the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What carried you to kill offspring. They said: O Messenger of Allah, they were only children of polytheists. He said: Are your best except children of polytheists. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, no soul is born except upon the natural disposition until its tongue expresses from it."
"15674","Ismail said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and raided with him, and gained mounts. So the people killed that day until they killed children, and once he said: offspring. So that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: What is with peoples, killing exceeded them today until they killed offspring. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, they are only children of polytheists. So he said: Indeed your best are sons of polytheists. Then he said: Indeed do not kill offspring, indeed do not kill offspring. He said: Every soul is born upon the natural disposition until its tongue expresses from it, then its parents make it Jewish and make it Christian."
"15675","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, that al-Aswad ibn Sari said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have praised my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, with praises and eulogies, and you. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, loves praise. Bring what you praised your Lord with. He said: So I began reciting to him, and a man came and sought permission, dark, bald, left-handed. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, silenced me for him, and Abu Salamah described for us how he silenced him, as one does with a cat. So the man entered and spoke a while then left, then I took reciting to him again, then he returned after, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, silenced me, and he described him also. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, who is this for whom you silenced me. So he said: This is a man who does not love falsehood. This is Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"15676","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned the hadith."
"16408","He said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an expedition on the day of Hunayn. Rawh said: So they came to a clan of the Arabs, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no soul born except upon the fitra, until its tongue expresses on its behalf."
"16409","He said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have praised Allah with one praise and praised you with another. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring it, and begin with the praise of Allah, Exalted and Majestic."
"16410","He said: Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Four on the Day of Resurrection: a deaf man who hears nothing, a foolish man, an aged man, and a man who died in the fatra. As for the deaf, he will say: Lord, Islam came and I heard nothing. As for the foolish, he will say: Lord, Islam came and the boys pelted me with dung. As for the aged, he will say: My Lord, Islam came and I understood nothing. As for the one who died in the fatra, he will say: Lord, no messenger of Yours came to me. Then He will take their covenants that they will obey Him, and He will send to them: Enter the Fire. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if they entered it, it would be coolness and safety upon them. He said:"
"16411","Ali narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayra, the like of this, except that he said at its end: Whoever enters it, it will be coolness and safety upon him, and whoever does not enter it will be dragged to it."
"16412","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, and he was a man of Banu Sa'd, he said: And he was the first who told stories in this mosque, meaning the congregational mosque. He said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, four raids. He said: So some people attacked the offspring after they had killed the fighters, and that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Lo, what is with some people who killed the fighters until they attacked the offspring. He said: So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not the children of the polytheists. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your best are the children of the polytheists. There is no soul born except it is born upon the fitra, and it remains upon it until its tongue makes clear on its behalf, then its parents make it a Jew or make it a Christian. He said: And al-Hasan concealed it."
